    "main": {
      "title": "HOW EASILY CAN SOMEONE CONTROL YOUR MIND?",
      "leadIn": 0.8,
      "tail": 5.0,
      "highlights": {
        "red": ["control", "manipulation", "manipulator", "scariest", "wrong", "pressure", "lie", "guilty", "afraid", "fear", "guilt", "gaslighting", "damaging", "harmful", "damage", "misinformation", "doubt"],
        "yellow": ["decisions", "experiment", "belong", "Asch", "conformity", "familiar", "Illusory", "Truth", "Effect", "repetition", "emotions", "insecurity", "excitement", "memory", "memories", "judgment", "pattern", "choice", "evidence", "independently", "FACTMAN", "everything", "curious", "Pause", "Question"]
      },
      "scenes": [
        {"id": "hook", "music": "dark", "lines": [
          {"id": "h1", "text": "Imagine someone could control your decisions without touching you, threatening you, or even speaking to you.", "rate": "-8%", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "h2", "text": "They could make you buy things you don't need, believe things that aren't true, and even doubt your own memories.", "rate": "-4%", "pause": 0.7},
          {"id": "h3", "text": "And the scariest part?", "rate": "-10%", "pause": 1.0},
          {"id": "h4", "text": "You might think all those decisions were yours.", "rate": "-10%", "pause": 0.9},
          {"id": "h5", "text": "Welcome to the hidden world of psychological manipulation.", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 4.2}
        ]},
        {"id": "setup", "music": "suspense", "lines": [
          {"id": "s1", "text": "Let's try a little experiment.", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "s2", "text": "Imagine you're walking into a room.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "s3", "text": "There are ten people inside.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "s4", "text": "They all point towards a completely ordinary object and confidently tell you it's something different.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "s5", "text": "You know they're wrong.", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "s6", "text": "But suddenly, you start questioning yourself.", "pause": 0.7},
          {"id": "s7", "text": "Why?", "pause": 0.8},
          {"id": "s8", "text": "Because your brain doesn't just want to be correct.", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "s9", "text": "It also wants to belong.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "s10", "text": "And that's where the first psychological trick begins.", "pause": 0.9}
        ]},
        {"id": "conformity", "music": "suspense", "leadIn": 1.8, "lines": [
          {"id": "c1", "text": "Humans are social creatures.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "c2", "text": "We naturally observe other people to understand how we should behave.", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "c3", "text": "In the famous Asch conformity experiments, participants sometimes gave incorrect answers about the lengths of lines simply because other people in the group had already given those answers.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "c4", "text": "Think about that.", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "c5", "text": "The correct answer was right in front of them.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "c6", "text": "Yet social pressure influenced their responses.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "c7", "text": "This is called conformity.", "rate": "-4%", "pause": 0.8},
          {"id": "c8", "text": "And it happens in everyday life.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "c9", "text": "Fashion trends. Social media opinions. Popular beliefs.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "c10", "text": "Sometimes, we don't follow something because we genuinely like it.", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "c11", "text": "We follow it because everyone else seems to.", "pause": 0.9}
        ]},
        {"id": "illusory", "music": "pulse", "leadIn": 1.8, "lines": [
          {"id": "i1", "text": "Now imagine hearing the same statement every single day.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "i2", "text": "At first, you don't believe it.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "i3", "text": "But after hearing it hundreds of times, it starts sounding familiar.", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "i4", "text": "And strangely, familiar information can sometimes feel more believable.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "i5", "text": "Psychologists call this the Illusory Truth Effect.", "pause": 0.8},
          {"id": "i6", "text": "It's one reason repetition is so powerful in advertising and misinformation.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "i7", "text": "But remember:", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "i8", "text": "Hearing something a thousand times doesn't make it true.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "i9", "text": "It only makes it familiar.", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 0.9}
        ]},
        {"id": "emotion", "music": "tense", "leadIn": 1.8, "lines": [
          {"id": "e1", "text": "Here's another way people influence your decisions.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "e2", "text": "They don't attack your logic.", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "e3", "text": "They target your emotions.", "pause": 0.7},
          {"id": "e4", "text": "Imagine someone makes you feel guilty whenever you disagree with them.", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "e5", "text": "Or makes you afraid of losing them whenever you set a boundary.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "e6", "text": "Eventually, you might start doing things just to avoid feeling guilty or afraid.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "e7", "text": "This is emotional manipulation.", "pause": 0.7},
          {"id": "e8", "text": "Fear, guilt, insecurity and even excitement can influence how we make decisions.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "e9", "text": "And when someone understands which emotions affect you most, they may use those emotions to pressure you.", "pause": 0.9}
        ]},
        {"id": "gaslighting", "music": "tense", "leadIn": 1.8, "lines": [
          {"id": "g1", "text": "Now comes one of the most damaging forms of manipulation.", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "g2", "text": "Gaslighting.", "rate": "-12%", "pause": 1.0},
          {"id": "g3", "text": "Imagine someone repeatedly denies things they said or did.", "rate": "-5%", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "g4", "text": "They tell you that you're remembering everything incorrectly.", "rate": "-5%", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "g5", "text": "They make you question your own experiences.", "rate": "-5%", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "g6", "text": "And slowly, you begin trusting their version of events more than your own memory.", "rate": "-5%", "pause": 0.7},
          {"id": "g7", "text": "That's why gaslighting can be so harmful.", "rate": "-5%", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "g8", "text": "It doesn't just create confusion.", "rate": "-5%", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "g9", "text": "It can damage your confidence in your own judgment.", "rate": "-5%", "pause": 0.7},
          {"id": "g10", "text": "But remember, one disagreement or different memory isn't automatically gaslighting.", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "g11", "text": "It's the repeated pattern of manipulation that matters.", "pause": 1.0}
        ]},
        {"id": "reveal", "music": "build", "lines": [
          {"id": "r1", "text": "So, can someone actually control your mind?", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 0.9},
          {"id": "r2", "text": "Not like a remote control.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "r3", "text": "But they can influence what you notice, what you believe, how you feel and sometimes what you decide.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "r4", "text": "And here's the interesting part.", "pause": 0.3},
          {"id": "r5", "text": "You don't need a mysterious hypnotist or a master manipulator for this to happen.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "r6", "text": "Advertising, social pressure, online trends and everyday relationships can all influence human behaviour.", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "r7", "text": "Sometimes, the strongest manipulation doesn't look like control.", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "r8", "text": "It looks like your own choice.", "rate": "-8%", "pause": 2.6}
        ]},
        {"id": "ending", "music": "inspire", "lines": [
          {"id": "n1", "text": "So how do you protect yourself?", "pause": 0.6},
          {"id": "n2", "text": "Pause before making emotional decisions.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "n3", "text": "Question information, even when everyone agrees with it.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "n4", "text": "Look for evidence instead of blindly trusting repetition.", "pause": 0.4},
          {"id": "n5", "text": "And never let someone make you feel guilty for thinking independently.", "pause": 0.8},
          {"id": "n6", "text": "Because the moment you stop questioning your decisions...", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "n7", "text": "Is the moment someone else can start making them for you.", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 1.2},
          {"id": "n8", "text": "This is FACTMAN.", "say": "This is Fact Man.", "rate": "-4%", "pause": 0.5},
          {"id": "n9", "text": "Stay curious. Question everything.", "rate": "-6%", "pause": 0.0}
        ]}
      ],
